- op: discuss  # 270c
  at: '2026-05-30T08:53:17Z'  # 270c
  by: agent  # 270c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 270c
  clock: 3  # 270c
  nonce: 270c  # 270c
  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, deeper-issue investigation): Largely closed-by-design — websocket.py:655-694 explicitly folds kind=\"websocket_endpoint\" to kind=\"function\" + meta[\"framework_role\"]=\"websocket_endpoint\" per ADR-0027 Phase 3 / audit-findings 0013 (\"Symbol.kind framework-role leak — mechanism vs. category\"). Tracker item predates the fix. Sibling to WI-lomoz (the other half of the WS taxonomy story — entrypoints vs usage_contexts vocabulary split). The remaining open question is the language=python half: for synthetic protocol nodes (kafka:/redis:/ws: prefix) there is no source language; the current code picks the emitter-file's language but a sentinel like \"framework\" or per-protocol value might be cleaner. The language axis is catalog-derived per ADR-0024 §4 with no policy for synthetic protocol nodes — candidate for an audit-findings extension. Moving to pending_validation for the kind=function half; language= question remains."  # 270c
