  clock: 9  # 842b
  nonce: 842b  # 842b
  message: "DONE per bulk-verify 2026-07-17: the owner-ruled fix (synthetic protocol stand-in nodes -> language=None + discovery_language + protocol_origin; register pt.9 Decision 2) is ALREADY IMPLEMENTED by the ADR-0031 rollout (post-dating the 2026-05-28 filing). Evidence: (1) 3-agent + dogfood scan -- every protocol_origin-bearing synthetic node in hypergumbo-core emits language=None + discovery_language (36 nodes, 0 defect sites); language='python' sites are all non-bugs (pattern dataclasses feeding discovery_language, or real Class-A source symbols). (2) GUARDED: spec_validator._check_cross_field_coherence (wired spec_validator.py:239, catalog line 148) flags any node with both language AND protocol_origin set + requires discovery_language on Class-B; TESTED by test_spec_validator_smoke.py::test_cross_field_flags_class_a_with_protocol_origin + test_cross_field_class_b_coherent_passes. (3) kind=function half already closed-by-design (ADR-0027 Phase 3, websocket.py:655-694). (4) Guard satisfied: no consumer hard-requires a real language (entrypoints.py:921 None-guarded, fingerprint.py None-safe). Adjacent (separate, NOT this item): HTTP route nodes (framework_role=route, analyzer-created) carry language=python -- defensibly Class-A real-source declarations, not the kafka/redis/ws/graphql synthetic families this item enumerates."  # 842b
